Unmatched routes get 404 {"error": "ROUTE NOT FOUND IN THIS REALM"}
(Requirement 7.8). Not pinned by the spec, so not tested: what a known path
with the wrong method gets (404 or 405).

### unknown path
GET /nowhere
=> 404

{"error": "ROUTE NOT FOUND IN THIS REALM"}

### unknown nested path, with a query
GET /hello/there/ghost?x=1
=> 404

{"error": "ROUTE NOT FOUND IN THIS REALM"}

### a route is not a prefix
GET /hellooo
=> 404

{"error": "ROUTE NOT FOUND IN THIS REALM"}

### the route itself still works
GET /hello
=> 200

{"message": "HELLO WORLD"}
